 75CU c  2012Ka36: {+238}U beam at E=345 MeV/nucleon provided by the RIBF       
 75CU2c  accelerator complex at RIKEN facility. Fission fragments were          
 75CU3c  separated and analyzed by BigRIPS separator, transported to focal      
 75CU4c  plane of ZeroDegree spectrometer and implanted in an aluminum stopper. 
 75CU5c  Particle identification was achieved by |DE-tof-B|r method.            
 75CU6c  5.4|*10{+5} {+75}Cu fragments were implanted.                          
 75CU6c  Delayed gamma rays from microsecond isomers were detected by three     
 75CU7c  clover-type HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, isomer       
 75CU8c  half-life. Deduced levels. Comparison with previous studies.           
 75CU c  The authors of 2012Ka36 use the level scheme from 2010Da06. However,   
 75CU2c  we use here the level scheme adopted from 2013Pe03.                    
